OL,3,GNEWSANuclear veteran says investigation
OL,4,Aa 'magical moment'                     
OL,6,FA nuclear test veteran who developed   
OL,7,Fcancer and lost his four-month-old son,
OL,8,Fhas said hearing an independent panel  
OL,9,Fwill look into Britain's atomic        
OL,10,Fprogramme was "a magical moment".      
OL,12,FJohn Morris, from Rochdale, was sent to
OL,13,FChristmas Island in the 1950s to work  
OL,14,Fon the UK's growing nuclear programme -
OL,15,Fand now believes the loss of his son   
OL,16,Fwas due to radiation exposure picked up
OL,17,Fon the island.                         
OL,19,FIt comes after Prime Minister Andy     
OL,20,FBurnham announced an investigation into
OL,21,Fthe lasting health impacts of testing  
OL,22,Fexercises in the 1950s and 60s.        
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
